# Scene 4: built on CsCheck, not instead of it. The same Order tested with plain CsCheck, every property by hand, beside
# the one line that drives every axis the rules declare.
Import //reels/entities.reelpreset
Screen code

Output //.artifacts/reel/scenes/04-one-line.mp4
Set Viewport 1600x900
Set FontSize 18

Code //tests/Nullean.Entities.Quickstart.Tests/PlainCsCheckTests.cs at "Gen<OrderLine>"
Say@skeptic "I already do property testing. I use CsCheck."
Say "Good. So does Entities. Here's the order tested with plain CsCheck."
Focus lines 29-37
Say "Good code. But every property is written by hand: the inputs, the law, the comparison, for every rule you thought of."
Focus off
Split //tests/Nullean.Entities.Quickstart.Tests/QuickstartTests.cs at "Gen<OrderLine>"
Link "Gen<Order> Orders" -> "Gen<Order> Orders" "the same CsCheck Gen"
Say "With Entities, the generator stays. What goes is the property."
Link "Cancelling_twice_is_cancelling_once" -> "EveryDeclaredAxisHolds" "declared as Idempotent"
Link "No_operation_lowers_the_version" -> "EveryDeclaredAxisHolds" "declared as Monotonic"
Link "The_total_is_never_negative" -> "EveryDeclaredAxisHolds" "declared as Always"
Say "The rule is the property. One line runs a case for every axis the rules declare, against every public method that returns an order."
Say@skeptic "Even one I add next month?"
Say "Even that one. No new test code."
Link off
Split off
Sleep 300ms
